{{fbdoc item="title" value="Sound Library Reference"}}----
Procedures, command families, examples, and backend notes for FreeBASIC's built-in sound library.

{{fbdoc item="desc"}}
	The sound library, or ##sfxlib##, is the built-in audio layer used by FreeBASIC's new sound commands. It covers generated tones, PLAY-string music, short sound effects, music file playback, MIDI commands, output device selection, and audio capture where the target backend supports it.

	Programs that use these commands automatically request the sfxlib runtime. If a program does not use the sound command surface and needs words such as ##Music##, ##Sfx##, or ##Device## as normal identifiers, define ##[[KeyPgFbNoSfxlib|FB_NO_SFXLIB]]## before those names are parsed.

{{fbdoc item="section" value="How sfxlib is arranged"}}
	Generated sound commands create tones, notes, PLAY strings, waveforms, envelopes, and instruments. The ##MUSIC## family controls one current music stream. The ##SFX## family loads and plays short reusable samples. ##MIDI## sends MIDI commands where a backend supports MIDI. ##DEVICE## selects the output backend, and ##CAPTURE## records input where capture support exists.

	For headless tests and package smoke tests, set ##SFXLIB_DRIVER=null## before the program starts to use the null output driver.

{{fbdoc item="section" value="Quick example"}}
%%(freebasic)
' generated tone
sound 440, 0.25

' PLAY-string phrase
play "t140 o4 cdefgab"

' short reusable sample
sfx load 1, "click.wav"
sfx play 1

sleep 1000, 1
%%

{{fbdoc item="section" value="Generated Sound"}}
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgBeep|BEEP"}}==
		Produces a beep or short pitched note.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSound|SOUND"}}==
		Plays a generated tone.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgTone|TONE"}}==
		Plays a generated tone on a selected channel.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgNoise|NOISE"}}==
		Plays generated noise.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgNote|NOTE"}}==
		Plays a named musical note.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgPlay|PLAY"}}==
		Plays BASIC PLAY strings.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgTempo|TEMPO"}}==
		Sets or returns PLAY-string tempo.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgChannel|CHANNEL"}}==
		Sets or returns the default generated-sound channel.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgOctave|OCTAVE"}}==
		Sets or returns the default note octave.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgVoice|VOICE"}}==
		Sets or returns the default instrument.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgVol|VOL"}}==
		Sets master volume.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgVolume|VOLUME"}}==
		Sets or returns master or channel volume.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgBalance|BALANCE"}}==
		Sets or returns master stereo balance.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgPan|PAN"}}==
		Sets or returns channel stereo pan.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgWave|WAVE"}}==
		Defines a generated waveform.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgEnvelope|ENVELOPE"}}==
		Defines an ADSR envelope.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgInstrument|INSTRUMENT"}}==
		Defines or assigns an instrument.

{{fbdoc item="section" value="Digital Audio and MIDI"}}
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgMusic|MUSIC"}}==
		Loads, plays, loops, pauses, resumes, stops, and queries the current music stream.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfx|SFX"}}==
		Loads and controls short sound effects by id or channel.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgMidi|MIDI"}}==
		Opens MIDI output, plays MIDI files, and sends MIDI messages where supported.

{{fbdoc item="section" value="Devices, Backends, and Capture"}}
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgDevice|DEVICE"}}==
		Lists, selects, and queries sfxlib output devices.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgSfxBackends|sfxlib backends"}}==
		Summarizes the output backends used on supported targets.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="KeyPgCapture|CAPTURE"}}==
		Starts, pauses, resumes, stops, reads, and saves audio capture where available.
	=={{fbdoc item="keyword" value="ProPgSfxAdvanced|Advanced sfxlib headers"}}==
		Documents raw PCM output, underrun and sample-rate queries, final-output WAV recording, and whole-mix echo.

